ts=2026-09-11T16:08:12.283Z type=preference scope=user content="preferred model per workspace.\n\nRemember preferred provider per project.\n\nPART 3 — COMMAND PALETTE\n\nImplement a professional command palette.\n\nShortcut:\n\nCtrl + K\n\nEverything searchable.\n\nChats\n\nProjects\n\nPrompts\n\nMemory\n\nModels\n\nProviders\n\nCommands\n\nSettings\n\nActions\n\nRecent files\n\nQuick create\n\nQuick switch\n\nRecent searches\n\nKeyboard-first navigation.\n\nPART 4 — GLOBAL SEARCH\n\nSearch absolutely everything.\n\nChats\n\nMessages\n\nPrompts\n\nWorkspace files\n\nMemory\n\nProjects\n\nTerminal history\n\nUsage\n\nSettings\n\nProvider names\n\nModel names\n\nResults grouped by category.\n\nInstant filtering.\n\nPART 5 — WORKSPACE INTELLIGENCE\n\nWhen a workspace opens:\n\nAutomatically index it.\n\nUnderstand:\n\nFiles\n\nFolders\n\nLanguages\n\nGit repository\n\nPackage managers\n\nDependencies\n\nREADME\n\nArchitecture\n\nRemember project context.\n\nNever ask repeatedly.\n\nPART 6 — SMART CONTEXT\n\nBefore every request automatically build context from:\n\nConversation\n\nWorkspace\n\nRelevant memory\n\nPinned prompts\n\nProject information\n\nRecent edits\n\nKeep context efficient.\n\nAvoid token waste.\n\nPART 7 — PROFESSIONAL UI\n\nRedesign the interface.\n\nCurrent UI is functional.\n\nNow make it premium.\n\nNo box-on-box layout.\n\nLarge spacing.\n\nElegant typography.\n\nBetter hierarchy.\n\nBeautiful hover states.\n\nMicro animations.\n\nSmooth transitions.\n\nFloating panels.\n\nPremium command center.\n\nModern sidebar.\n\nModern chat.\n\nModern markdown.\n\nBeautiful code blocks.\n\nProfessional loading states.\n\nProfessional empty states.\n\nProfessional onboarding.\n\nEverything should feel like premium software.\n\nPART 8 — PERFORMANCE\n\nOptimize everything.\n\nLazy loading.\n\nMemoization.\n\nDatabase queries.\n\nRendering.\n\nScrolling.\n\nLarge chats.\n\nWorkspace indexing.\n\nSearch.\n\nStartup speed.\n\nMemory usage.\n\nPART 9 — PRODUCTIVITY\n\nAdd:\n\nPinned chats\n\nPinned prompts\n\nFavorite models\n\nRecent workspaces\n\nQuick reopen\n\nSession restore\n\nRecent files\n\nDrag-and-drop improvements\n\nBetter keyboard shortcuts\n\nCommand history\n\nPART 10 — CODING WORKSPACE\n\nImprove coding experience.\n\nBetter terminal.\n\nBetter git status.\n\nBetter file previews.\n\nBetter diff viewer.\n\nBetter markdown preview.\n\nSafer command approval.\n\nBetter workspace explorer.\n\nPART 11 — SETTINGS\n\nProfessional settings.\n\nSearchable.\n\nCategorized.\n\nImport/export.\n\nBackup.\n\nRestore.\n\nProvider diagnostics.\n\nSystem information.\n\nDatabase information.\n\nWorkspace information.\n\nPerformance statistics.\n\nPART 12 — STABILITY\n\nRun verification continuously.\n\nAfter each major section:\n\nBuild.\n\nLaunch.\n\nSmoke test.\n\nFix errors immediately.\n\nNever continue while broken.\n\nPART 13 — CODE QUALITY\n\nRefactor duplicated logic.\n\nImprove typings.\n\nImprove architecture.\n\nImprove readability.\n\nImprove maintainability.\n\nDo not over-engineer.\n\nPART 14 — FUTURE READY\n\nDesign extension points for:\n\nPlugins\n\nMCP\n\nVoice\n\nVision\n\nAutomation\n\nMultiple agents\n\nCloud sync (optional)\n\nWithout implementing everything now.\n\nDESIGN LANGUAGE\n\nThe UI must inherit the Fluxora brand.\n\nPremium.\n\nMinimal.\n\nElegant.\n\nTimeless.\n\nFast.\n\nProfessional.\n\nConsistent.\n\nNo generic dashboard appearance.\n\nLOGO\n\nDo NOT redesign the Fluxora logo.\n\nTreat the existing logo as the official brand identity.\n\nOnly improve integration:\n\nSplash screen\n\nWindow icon\n\nTaskbar\n\nInstaller\n\nAbout screen\n\nLoading screen\n\nWallpaper\n\nBrand consistency\n\nFINAL VALIDATION\n\nBefore finishing:\n\nRun full build.\n\nRun smoke launch.\n\nVerify:\n\nNo TypeScript errors.\n\nNo IPC errors.\n\nNo runtime exceptions.\n\nNo missing providers.\n\nNo broken streaming.\n\nNo broken persistence.\n\nNo broken encryption.\n\nNo broken workspace functionality.\n\nNo broken chats.\n\nNo broken memories.\n\nNo broken prompts.\n\nNo broken settings.\n\nEverything must pass.\n\nFINAL REPORT\n\nGenerate a comprehensive report containing:\n\nFeatures implemented\nFiles modified\nArchitecture changes\nPerformance improvements\nSecurity improvements\nUI improvements\nRemaining limitations\nFuture recommendations\nBuild status\nTest status\nProduction readiness score (0–100)\nSuggested next milestone\n\nDo not stop after implementing one feature. Continue until every task above is complete, keeping the application functional throughout." tags=auto
